    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2RR5QbbYJjj1sFV7GqnnTRu)_\n\n**Before:** `docs/architecture/load-order-*.svg` were committed and re-rendered on every edit, so open PRs conflicted on them.\n\n**After:**\n- `docs/Makefile`: `make -C .config/emacs-modular/docs docs` extracts every `#+begin_src dot ... :file NAME.svg` block from the Org docs and runs `dot -Tsvg`, writing the SVG next to the `.org` file (so `[[file:...svg]]` links work locally). Needs Graphviz.\n- The two SVGs are removed from git; `docs/**/*.svg` and `docs/.build/` are in `.gitignore`.\n- `.github/workflows/docs-svg.yml`: on PRs it only checks every block renders; on push to `main` it force-pushes the SVGs to an orphan `docs-assets` branch (same relative paths). That is how the files \"show up in the repo\".\n- ADR 0011 compares the options (artifact only, GitHub Pages, committing from CI, status quo) and picks the branch; CHANGELOG entry and a note in `load-order.org`.\n\n**Open PRs (#54, #58, #72/#73):** once this merges, merging `main` into them will conflict only if they edit the SVG files. Resolve with `git rm` of both SVGs (keep the `dot` change in the `.org`); the SVG is then rebuilt by make.\n\n**Checked:** the block extraction (both blocks come out as the right `.dot` files) with a stub `dot`. **Not checked:** real `dot` rendering (not installed here) and the workflow itself; the `docs-assets` branch appears after the first push to `main`. The workflow needs Actions write permission (set in the file).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ey7PatqEncqfxdQMmJdGZr)_",
